The MIT licence above covers the Mote engine, SDK, tools, Studio and the games
written for it, EXCEPT for the following, which carry their own terms:

* games/moria/
    A port of Umoria 5.6.0, Copyright (C) 1989-2008 James E. Wilson,
    Robert A. Koeneke, David J. Grabiner. Licensed under the GNU General Public
    License, version 3 or later. The whole of games/moria/ -- including the
    Mote-specific files written for the port -- is GPLv3, and any binary built
    from it (Moria.mote) must be conveyed under the GPL.
    See games/moria/COPYING and games/moria/README.md.

* studio/third_party/
    stb_image.h and stb_image_write.h by Sean Barrett -- public domain
    (or MIT, at your option). See the licence block at the end of each file.

Individual games may also incorporate third-party art or audio packs under
their own terms; where that is the case it is credited in the game's directory
and in its gallery description. Notably:

* games/roguemote/ uses the "Simple Roguelike Tileset" by Ink_Slime --
  CC0 / public domain. See games/roguemote/ASSETS.md.
* games/kingsandpigs/ uses a free art pack by Pixel Frog.

Because games/moria/ is GPLv3 and the rest of the repository is MIT, the two
are compatible in one direction only: MIT-licensed engine and SDK code may be
combined into the GPLv3 Moria binary, but Moria's GPL code may not be copied
back into the MIT-licensed parts of the tree.
